us suggests reliability. Stress handling good. Weather assessment technical. Computer skills technical. Grumpy/uncooperative may affect crew cooperation and communication.\n\nCandidate C: strengths: can make correct decisions quickly, 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere with crew. Concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education. Reliability excellent, decision quality good, crew atmosphere positive, but communication difficulty and egocentric may affect cooperation. Lack of willingness to further education may affect adaptability.\n\nCandidate D: strengths: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Concerns: regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership skills. So good problem solving, attention, responsibility, but arrogance and weak leadership may affect crew cooperation.\n\nWe need best overall fit. Candidate C seems strong on reliability, decision quality, crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric may be serious for cockpit. Candidate B strong on stress, conscientiousness, but uncooperative. Candidate A strong technical, leadership but unorganized and poor criticism acceptance. Candidate D strong problem solving, attention, responsibility but arrogance and weak leadership.\n\nWhich is best overall? Probably Candidate C, because reliability and decision quality are critical, and positive crew atmosphere suggests cooperation despite communication difficulty? But difficulty communicating ideas is a safety risk. Egocentric also risk. Candidate B's stress handling and conscientiousness are important, but uncooperative may be severe. Candidate A's unorganized may affect reliability. Candidate D's arrogance may affect crew.\n\nI think Candidate C is strongest overall despite communication concerns; but we need to weigh. Maybe we should ask another panel member about candidate C's communication difficulty impact. But we can still make a recommendation now.\n\nWe need to reference existing discussion: none, but we can say \"Given the initial overview\".\n\nWe'll state vote for Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
